Subject: [PATCH] sixaxis: fall back to VID/PID matching for clone controllers

Many third-party DualShock 3 clones reuse Sony's 054c:0268 IDs but report
unusual USB product names ("ShanWan PS(R) Ga`epad", "Gasia Co.,Ltd PS(R)
Gamepad", ...). get_pairing() only accepts the names listed in its table, so
the sixaxis plugin ignores them and cable pairing never happens.

When no entry matches by name, fall back to the first CABLE_PAIRING_SIXAXIS
entry with the same VID/PID.

Tested on BlueZ 5.85 with 3 ShanWan and 1 Gasia clones.
---
--- a/profiles/input/sixaxis.h
+++ b/profiles/input/sixaxis.h
@@ -73,6 +73,7 @@
 			.type = CABLE_PAIRING_DS4,
 		},
 	};
+	const struct cable_pairing *fallback = NULL;
 	guint i;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < G_N_ELEMENTS(devices); i++) {
@@ -81,13 +82,22 @@
 		if (devices[i].pid != pid)
 			continue;
 
-		if (name && !g_str_has_suffix(name, devices[i].name))
+		if (name && !g_str_has_suffix(name, devices[i].name)) {
+			/* Many third-party Sixaxis clones reuse Sony's VID/PID
+			 * but report odd product names (e.g. "ShanWan PS(R)
+			 * Ga`epad"). They speak the same protocol, so fall
+			 * back to the first entry matching the VID/PID.
+			 */
+			if (!fallback &&
+				devices[i].type == CABLE_PAIRING_SIXAXIS)
+				fallback = &devices[i];
 			continue;
+		}
 
 		return &devices[i];
 	}
 
-	return NULL;
+	return fallback;
 }
 
 #endif /* _SIXAXIS_H_ */
